From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: sunxi: sun55i-pck600: set pd->pck, or the error path oopses

sunxi_pck600_pd_set_power() opens with

	struct sunxi_pck600 *pck = pd->pck;

and uses it once, in the failure branch:

	if (ret)
		dev_err(pck->dev, "failed to turn domain \"%s\" %s: %d\n", ...);

but nothing ever assigns pd->pck. The field exists in struct
sunxi_pck600_pd and the probe loop fills in genpd.name, the two callbacks
and base, and skips it. So every failing power transition dereferences
NULL in the very line that was meant to explain the failure.

The dev_err is the only reader of pd->pck, so the NULL is only reached
when a power transition actually fails. Nothing here claims anything about
A523 hardware -- that part is not ours to assert. What is measured is this
SoC: on the A733, PWPR moves a domain in both directions, verified on VI
(index 0) on the 8 GiB board on 2026-09-07 with PWPR 0x8 -> PWSR 0x8 and PWPR
0x0 -> PWSR 0x0, each following within the read latency; and GPU_CORE is
the one domain where the identical write does nothing, so its PWSR poll
runs the full 10 ms, returns -ETIMEDOUT, and the driver walks straight
into the NULL.

Found at silicon, the 8 GiB board, 2026-09-07, with the GPU node
enabled and powervr binding:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0
  Internal error: Oops: 0000000096000004 [#1] SMP
  CPU: 7 PID: 250 Comm: (udev-worker)
  pc : sunxi_pck600_pd_set_power+0xac/0xe8
  lr : sunxi_pck600_power_on+0x14/0x20
  Call trace:
    sunxi_pck600_pd_set_power+0xac/0xe8 (P)
    sunxi_pck600_power_on+0x14/0x20
    _genpd_power_on / genpd_power_on / genpd_runtime_resume
    rpm_get_suppliers
    pvr_device_init+0x100/0x5b8 [powervr]
    pvr_probe+0xd8/0x14c [powervr]

One line. It also matters beyond the crash: with pd->pck NULL the driver
could never have printed which domain failed, which is the whole content
of that dev_err.

Falsifier: on the same image, the GPU node enabled and powervr loaded,
the probe fails with 'failed to turn domain "GPU_CORE" on: -110' on the
console and no oops.

Present unchanged in torvalds/master (df2908090cda, 7.3-rc2), in
linux-next and in the pmdomain maintainer tree ulfh/linux-pm.git#next --
all three byte-identical, two `pck =` matches in the file and neither of
them assigning pd->pck. No fix and no report found in patchwork or in the
git history (lore itself was not searched): patchwork q=pck600 returns only
the three known series (A523, A733, flags), and the file's whole history is
those three commits.

Fixes: 76e4310115ca ("pmdomain: sunxi: add driver for Allwinner A523's PCK-600 power controller")
Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
@@ -194,6 +194,7 @@
 		struct sunxi_pck600_pd *pd = &pck->pds[i];
 		bool is_off;
 
+		pd->pck = pck;
 		pd->genpd.name = desc->pd_names[i];
 		pd->genpd.power_off = sunxi_pck600_power_off;
 		pd->genpd.power_on = sunxi_pck600_power_on;
